---
// "Why this matters" - the problem section that sits after the hero. One sourced
// stat (docs are how devs learn), then a 2x2 of "current state" failure modes:
// stale, wrong audience, never written, and the AI version. Unified neutral
// chrome; red is reserved for the one broken thing inside each infographic, so
// the tiles read as a cohesive set of today's negatives rather than random color.
import Section from './Section.astro';

const SO = 'https://survey.stackoverflow.co/2024/';
---

<Section
  id="why-docs"
  eyebrow="Why this matters"
  title="Everyone needs the docs. Every way we make them is broken."
  tone="canvas"
>
  <!-- Single sourced claim -->
  <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-md items-center gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-paper p-5 shadow-soft">
    <span class="shrink-0 font-display text-[46px] font-extrabold leading-none gradient-text">84%</span>
    <p class="text-[14px] leading-snug text-ink-soft">
      of developers call technical documentation their number-one way to learn a new tool.
      <a
        href={SO}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        class="ml-0.5 inline-flex items-center gap-0.5 align-baseline font-mono text-[11px] text-muted underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-brand-600"
        >source<svg width="9" height="9" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17 17 7M9 7h8v8" /></svg></a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Framing: everything below is the current, broken state -->
  <div class="mt-11 flex justify-center">
    <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-danger/20 bg-danger/[0.06] px-3.5 py-1.5 text-[12.5px] font-medium text-danger">
      <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" /><path d="M9 9l6 6M15 9l-6 6" /></svg>
      How it goes today, without docstube
    </span>
  </div>

  <!-- 2x2 failure-mode tiles -->
  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <!-- Stale -->
    <div class="surface hover-lift flex flex-col gap-4 p-6 sm:p-7">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-ink/5 text-ink-soft ring-1 ring-inset ring-line">
          <svg width="21" height="21" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" /><path d="M12 8v4.5l3 1.8" /></svg>
        </span>
        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold text-ink">It goes stale</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Code ships every day; hand-written docs don't move. Signatures drift until the page is quietly describing an
        API that no longer exists.
      </p>
      <div class="flex h-[150px] flex-col justify-center gap-3 rounded-xl border border-line bg-canvas p-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-[68px] shrink-0 font-mono text-[9px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">the docs</span>
          <code class="flex-1 rounded-lg border border-line bg-paper px-3 py-2 font-mono text-[12.5px] text-muted line-through decoration-danger/70 decoration-2">getSession()</code>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-[68px] shrink-0 font-mono text-[9px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">the code</span>
          <code class="flex-1 rounded-lg border border-line bg-paper px-3 py-2 font-mono text-[12.5px] text-ink">getSession(<span class="text-brand-600">opts</span>)</code>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 text-danger">
          <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 9h14M5 15h14" /><path d="M18 4 6 20" /></svg>
          <span class="font-mono text-[10.5px] font-semibold">out of sync with the source</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Wrong audience -->
    <div class="surface hover-lift flex flex-col gap-4 p-6 sm:p-7">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-ink/5 text-ink-soft ring-1 ring-inset ring-line">
          <svg width="21" height="21" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 12s3.6-6.5 10-6.5S22 12 22 12" /><path d="M2 12s3.6 6.5 10 6.5S22 12 22 12" /><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2.5" /><path d="M4 20 20 4" /></svg>
        </span>
        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold text-ink">It assumes too much</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Whoever wrote the code can't un-know it. The obvious step gets skipped, internal names leak in, and the context
        a newcomer actually needs never makes it onto the page.
      </p>
      <div class="flex h-[150px] flex-col justify-center gap-3 rounded-xl border border-line bg-canvas p-4">
        <div class="w-fit max-w-[90%] rounded-2xl rounded-bl-sm border border-line bg-paper px-3 py-2 text-[12px] leading-snug text-ink-soft">
          Initialise the client with your <span class="rounded bg-ink/[0.06] px-1 text-ink">workspace token</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="ml-auto flex w-fit max-w-[92%] items-center gap-2 rounded-2xl rounded-br-sm border border-danger/25 bg-danger/[0.06] px-3 py-2 text-[12px] leading-snug text-danger">
          <span class="flex h-4 w-4 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-danger/15 text-[10px] font-bold">?</span>
          …what's a workspace token, and where do I get one?
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Never written -->
    <div class="surface hover-lift flex flex-col gap-4 p-6 sm:p-7">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-ink/5 text-ink-soft ring-1 ring-inset ring-line">
          <svg width="21" height="21" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 3v5h5" /><path d="M7 3h7l5 5v10a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2z" /><path d="M8.5 17 15 10.5" /><path d="M15 17 8.5 10.5" /></svg>
        </span>
        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold text-ink">It never gets written</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Docs are the chore that loses to every deadline. The easy pages get done; configuration, edge cases, and the
        gnarly migration — the ones readers need most — stay empty.
      </p>
      <div class="flex h-[150px] flex-col justify-center gap-2 rounded-xl border border-line bg-canvas p-4 font-mono text-[12px]">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-ink-soft"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" class="shrink-0 text-pass"><path d="M2.5 6.2 5 8.7 9.5 3.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg> Quickstart</div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-ink-soft"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" class="shrink-0 text-pass"><path d="M2.5 6.2 5 8.7 9.5 3.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg> Installation</div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-muted"><span class="shrink-0 text-line-strong">○</span> Configuration<span class="ml-auto rounded border border-dashed border-line-strong px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px]">empty</span></div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-muted"><span class="shrink-0 text-line-strong">○</span> Migration guide<span class="ml-auto rounded border border-dashed border-line-strong px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px]">empty</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- AI -->
    <div class="surface hover-lift flex flex-col gap-4 p-6 sm:p-7">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-ink/5 text-ink-soft ring-1 ring-inset ring-line">
          <svg width="21" height="21" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3l1.7 4.6L18 9l-4.3 1.4L12 15l-1.7-4.6L6 9l4.3-1.4L12 3z" /><path d="M18.5 13.5l.7 1.9 1.9.7-1.9.7-.7 1.9-.7-1.9-1.9-.7 1.9-.7.7-1.9z" /></svg>
        </span>
        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold text-ink">And AI doesn't fix it</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Point a model at your repo and the pages read beautifully. Check them against the source and the problems pour
        out — fluent, confident, and wrong.
      </p>
      <div class="flex h-[150px] flex-col justify-center gap-2.5 rounded-xl border border-line bg-canvas p-4">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="font-mono text-[10.5px] text-ink-soft">auth.mdx · AI draft</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-[10px] text-muted">reads perfectly</span>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-1.5 text-[11.5px] text-ink-soft">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="shrink-0 text-danger"><path d="M4 4l6 6M10 4l-6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" /></svg> <span class="font-mono text-ink">client.flush()</span> — no such method</div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="shrink-0 text-danger"><path d="M4 4l6 6M10 4l-6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" /></svg> two code samples contradict each other</div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="shrink-0 text-danger"><path d="M4 4l6 6M10 4l-6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" /></svg> a confident claim with nothing behind it</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
